Id: invalid-utf8-input
Title: Invalid UTF-8 input is an error
Input: Any string whose bytes are not valid UTF-8 once it has been
 converted by its mark, in a call to any exported function that takes
 text. For example the bytes 63 61 66 E9 marked as UTF-8, the bytes
 ED A0 80 (a lone surrogate, U+D800), or C0 80.
Reference: A Python string cannot hold arbitrary invalid bytes, so the
 nearest inputs are strings holding surrogate code points, which the
 reference version accepts. Run on ftfy 6.3.1 with Python 3.13:
 fix_text('caf\udce9') returns 'caf\ufffd', fix_text('\ud800') returns
 '\ufffd', and fix_encoding() returns both strings unchanged. Bytes
 given in place of text, as in fix_text(b'caf\xe9'), raise UnicodeError.
R: An error raised by the entry step, before any other work. The message
 says how many elements hold invalid UTF-8, names the positions of the
 first five, and says that the data was probably read with the wrong
 codec. No invalid input is repaired.
Decided: https://github.com/epabarker/r-ftfy/issues/12#issuecomment-6858969101
